From 6022ad0280f07e65aaf0becf70c0203e8d6f37de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman Semenoff <GermanAizek@yandex.ru>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 21:20:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] nvc0/nouveau: optimize mt nouveau and fermi/kepler driver

nouveau:
- Buffer object cache (BO recycling) has been added to struct nouveau_fence_list, eliminating frequent calls to DRM_IOCTL_NOUVEAU_GEM_NEW and GEM_CLOSE when creating a fence
- nouveau_fence_ref2 function has been added for batch updating paired references to read/write fences under single mutex
- locking of the mutex when resetting zero references to a fence has been eliminated

nvc0 (Fermi/Kepler):
- excessive PUSH_KICK calls during blit and clear operations have been eliminated; the pushbuf reset during context switching is limited by the condition ctx_from != ctx_to
- program code buffers (screen->text) and constant buffers (screen->uniform_bo) have been made permanently resident in bufctx_3d and bufctx_cp
- Caching of index buffer state (format, address, resource) has been implemented, which eliminates the need to rewrite 5 hardware registers when the index remains unchanged between draw calls
- Batch acquisition of the fence list mutex when validating resources in nvc0_bufctx_fence
- Skipping inactive and unchanged shader stages during sampler and texture validation
- optimized the constant loading path in pushbuf to use a single batch
